<Layout
  title={"RCE-JEPA: World Coding, with JEPA as Premise"}
  description={"About RCE-JEPA. World Coding is the subject; JEPA is the premise. Reports measured H1, H2 (C_check / E_model = 0.000582 on M5 Max), H5 & H11 on unseen Form shapes via FormEBM-v2 (5.85M params: AUROC 0.8922, 93.0% 5-step monotonicity), H7, H8, H14, H15 + FormJEPA-v1 (27/40 k=16) + H15-Iterative (40/40 on Opus 5.5 & Sonnet 5.5, 0 contradictions) + Shape D Gear-0 (40/40 at 0 calls, 16.67x 3-Gear Zipf reduction), and 151-task rce repair rung f promotion audit."}
>
  <section class="px-6 md:px-10 pt-16 md:pt-24 pb-20 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <p class="section-label mb-4">Research paper · about</p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-brand-white tracking-tight">
      RCE-JEPA: World Coding, with JEPA as Premise
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-6 font-body text-base text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      RCE-JEPA (RCE is the Reality Code Engine; JEPA is a Joint Embedding Predictive Architecture) keeps its name. The subject is World Coding. JEPA is the premise: predict a compact summary of a program instead of the next word-piece of text. The proposer slot is any learned model over Forms. The checker decides. The Laws of Coding are the acceptance rule under test.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-8 glass-card p-6">
      <p class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[2px] uppercase text-brand-gray mb-3">What it claims and what it does not</p>
      <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-2 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
        <li>It states a thesis, fifteen hypotheses (H1 to H15) and six falsifiers (RJ-F1 to RJ-F6). Measured deterministic floors: median rho <code>9.34</code> over 185 hand-written programs (H1); <code>0</code> invariant violations in 1,275 fuzzed mutants (H7); <code>0</code> replay mismatches on 10,500 streams across six targets (H8); and the plain arm of ladder run 3 closing <code>111</code> of <code>151</code> tasks (<code>73.5%</code>) at zero model calls, leaving <code>40</code> real-history residual tasks (H14 supported).</li>
        <li>At <code>openIE-dev/rce</code> commit <code>1762fb4b</code> (<code>reported_j</code>; <code>measured_j = None</code>, <code>board_metered = false</code>): <strong>H2 is supported</strong> on Apple M5 Max (<code>C_check / E_model = 0.04904 J / 84.25 J = 0.000582 &lt;= 0.05</code>, <code>1,718×</code> cheaper). On the strictly disjoint <code>1,387</code>-Form split (zero task overlap), <strong><code>FormJEPA-v1</code></strong> (<code>8.42M</code> parameters) admits <code>177/200</code> held-out synthetic defects and <code>27/40</code> H15 tasks at <code>k = 16</code> (<code>474.76 mJ</code> RAPL core <code>reported_j</code>), while contrastive <strong><code>FormEBM-v2</code></strong> (<code>5.85M</code> parameters) reaches unseen-shape <strong>H5 AUROC <code>0.8922 &gt;= 0.85</code></strong> (<code>84.05%</code> solvable top-1 accuracy, <code>2.39×</code> fewer checker calls) and <strong>H11 <code>93.0% &gt;= 80%</code></strong> strict 5-step cumulative defect monotonicity (Spearman <code>0.9931</code>, <code>47.09 mJ</code>/candidate core <code>reported_j</code>).</li>
        <li>Across the <strong>40 open residual tasks</strong> (<strong>H15</strong>), single-shot proposers admit <code>17/40</code> to <code>34/40</code>, while bounded <code>&lt;= 5</code>-turn checker feedback plus public <code>stdlib/lib</code> signature headers (<strong><code>H15-Iterative</code></strong>, zero access to the original Form) closes <strong><code>40/40</code> (<code>100.0%</code>)</strong> on <code>Claude Opus 5.5</code> (<code>$1.81</code>) and <code>Claude Sonnet 5.5</code> (<code>$1.11</code>) with <strong><code>0</code> contradictions</strong> (<code>39/40</code> on <code>xAI Grok 4.20 Reasoning</code>). Crystallizing all 40 verified repairs into <strong>Shape D (<code>DNULLMM1</code>) Gear-0 v2</strong> replays <strong><code>40/40</code> at <code>0</code> calls</strong> (<code>0.325 µs</code> / <code>1.77 µJ</code> per probe), and the <strong>3-Gear Cascade</strong> admits <code>200/200</code> recurring <code>Zipf(0.85)</code> arrivals with <strong><code>16.67×</code> fewer Gear-2 episodes</strong> (<code>12</code> vs <code>200</code>). The 151-task <code>rce repair</code> rung <code>f</code> audit records <code>3/119 = 2.5% &gt; 2.0%</code> stochastic closes (<code>0</code> contradictions), keeping rung <code>f</code> in <code>observe</code> mode; full intent-to-Form synthesis (H3), multi-line out-of-distribution energy calibration (<code>0.2630</code> pooled AUROC), and external wall-meter <code>measured_j</code> remain open.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <figure class="mt-10 glass-card p-4 fig">
      <a class="fig-zoom" href="/figures/rce-jepa/three-gear-and-ebm.svg" aria-label="Enlarge figure"><img src="/figures/rce-jepa/three-gear-and-ebm.svg" alt="Measured Three-Gear residual cascade (40/40 warm DNULLMM1 replay, 200/200 Zipf(0.85) stream) alongside FormEBM-v2 H5 ROC curve (AUROC 0.8922) and H11 5-step energy landscape (93.0% strict monotonicity)." loading="lazy" /></a>
